# ~/.claude — synced between machines via the claude-config repo.
#
# ALLOWLIST, NOT DENYLIST. Claude Code and its plugins own this directory and
# add new subdirectories without warning — `chrome/` (the Claude-in-Chrome
# native host wrapper), `daemon/` (which holds control.key, a credential),
# `context-mode/`, `jobs/`, `feedback/` have all appeared here. A denylist has
# to be updated for each one, and every miss is committed silently: that is how
# a credential and four app-generated files nearly reached this remote.
#
# So: ignore everything, then re-include exactly what we deliberately track.
# A new app directory is now ignored by default. The failure mode flips from
# "secret leaks" to "you notice a file you wanted isn't tracked", which is the
# right way round.
#
# The rule for what earns a line below: commit CONFIGURATION, never STATE,
# never CREDENTIALS, and never a file another program generates (it would be
# overwritten by a checkout — see cmux/README.md on Claude Usage.app).

/*

!/.gitignore
!/README.md
!/settings.json
!/skills-manager.sh
!/skills/
!/skills-disabled/
!/cmux/

# ── exclusions inside the allowed trees ─────────────────────────────────────
# Per-machine cmux config: each laptop writes its own.
/cmux/config.local.sh
/cmux/config.local.sh.bak-*

# Skills the Claude app syncs down from the account. App-generated state inside
# an otherwise tracked tree: `!/skills/` re-included it, and a checkout would
# overwrite whatever the app had just written.
/skills/synced/

# Notes on things the allowlist now covers implicitly, kept so nobody re-adds
# them by hand:
#   daemon/                  holds control.key — a credential
#   chrome/                  Claude-in-Chrome native messaging host wrapper
#   statusline-command.sh    ) generated and rewritten by Claude Usage.app;
#   statusline-config.txt    ) committing them means a checkout clobbers the app
#   fetch-claude-usage.swift ) and this one embeds an sk-ant-sid session token
#   settings.local.json      never read at user level, but never commit it either
#   projects/ history.jsonl plugins/ file-history/ context-mode/   bulk state
